{{
As someone who certainly disagrees with the notion that birthplace automatically equates with national identity, it’s intriguing to encounter perspectives like yours, which lean toward agreement. While I appreciate how deeply rooted cultural ties might seem within native-born citizens, I feel compelled to share my viewpoint respectfully yet passionately.

For me, "being American" encompasses much more than geographical origin; instead, it reflects shared democratic ideals, such as equality before law, freedom of speech, and opportunity irrespective of race, gender,

